You are fixing an Important finding from Task 10's review, for the Chapters project (~/Documents/chapters, branch feat/ui-scaffold-auth).

## Finding

In `client/src/pages/auth/LoginPage.tsx`, the `attemptLogin` function's catch block treats every `mfaRequired` response the same way:

```ts
} catch (err) {
  if (isMfaRequired(err)) {
    setMfaChallenge(true)
  } else if (err instanceof ApiError) {
    setError(err.message)
  } else {
    setError('Something went wrong. Try again.')
  }
}
```

The backend returns `mfaRequired: true` in TWO distinct situations: (1) the very first login attempt with a correct password but no TOTP code yet ("totp code required" — this is normal, expected, not an error to show), and (2) a retry attempt that already included a TOTP code, but it was WRONG ("invalid totp code" — this IS an error the user needs to see). The current code can't tell these apart, so a wrong TOTP code produces zero visible feedback: the form just sits there looking the same, with no error shown, because `isMfaRequired(err)` is true in both cases and the `setError` branches are never reached.

## Your job

1. Read `client/src/pages/auth/LoginPage.tsx` in full to see the current `attemptLogin` function and its call sites (`handlePasswordSubmit` calls `attemptLogin(false)`, `handleTotpSubmit` calls `attemptLogin(true)`).
2. Fix the catch block to distinguish the two cases using the `withTotp` parameter already available in `attemptLogin(withTotp: boolean)`: when `isMfaRequired(err)` is true AND `withTotp` is true, that's a wrong-code retry — call `setError(err.message)` (or an appropriate fallback if `err` isn't an `ApiError` for some reason) in addition to keeping `setMfaChallenge(true)`. When `isMfaRequired(err)` is true and `withTotp` is false, that's the normal first-time MFA prompt — no error needed, same as today.
3. Read `client/src/pages/auth/LoginPage.test.tsx` to see the existing 3 test cases, then add a 4th test case: submit correct email/password (triggering the MFA prompt), then submit a WRONG totp code and assert (a) the error message renders (use the backend's real error text, `'invalid totp code'`, matching the pattern `server/src/auth/routes.ts` uses: `401 {error: 'invalid totp code', mfaRequired: true}`), and (b) the TOTP field is still shown (mfaChallenge stayed true — the form didn't bounce back to the password step). Follow the existing tests' style exactly (mockJsonResponse, fetchMock chaining with mockResolvedValueOnce, userEvent).
4. Run the test file, then the full suite, to confirm everything passes including your new test.
5. Run typecheck.

## Commit

Message: "Fix LoginPage: surface wrong-TOTP error instead of silently retrying"

## Report

Append your fix report (the exact diff of the catch block, the new test case's code, test results) to /Users/taha/Documents/chapters/.superpowers/sdd/task-10-report.md as a new "## Fix: surface wrong-TOTP error" section.

Then report back with ONLY (under 15 lines):
- Status: DONE | BLOCKED
- Commit created (short SHA + subject)
- One-line test summary (must include the new test count)
- The report file path

